---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import "../styles/content.css";
---

<BaseLayout title="Docs — Raohane" description="Raohane commands, configuration paths, launcher modes, troubleshooting and development notes.">
  <div class="page-shell">
    <SiteHeader active="docs" />
    <main class="content-main shell-width">
      <section class="page-intro">
        <span class="page-badge">Reference</span>
        <h1>Know the shell.<br/><em>Keep control.</em></h1>
        <p>A compact reference for daily use, configuration and recovery. Deeper architecture and release documentation stays in the source repository.</p>
      </section>

      <div class="docs-layout">
        <aside class="docs-nav" aria-label="Documentation sections">
          <a href="#commands">Commands</a>
          <a href="#launcher">Launcher</a>
          <a href="#configuration">Configuration</a>
          <a href="#themes">Themes</a>
          <a href="#diagnostics">Diagnostics</a>
          <a href="#development">Development</a>
        </aside>

        <article class="docs-article">
          <section id="commands">
            <span class="section-kicker">Daily use</span>
            <h2>Commands</h2>
            <p>The <code>raohane</code> CLI provides direct entry points for the primary surfaces.</p>
            <div class="code-panel"><pre><code>raohane launcher
raohane control
raohane settings
raohane media
raohane desktop
raohane wallpaper
raohane session
raohane translate</code></pre></div>
          </section>

          <section id="launcher">
            <span class="section-kicker">Search grammar</span>
            <h2>Launcher modes</h2>
            <p>The launcher is more than an application list. Prefixes switch the search model without opening another tool.</p>
            <ul>
              <li><code>/</code> — built-in Raohane actions.</li>
              <li><code>&gt;</code> — command execution.</li>
              <li><code>=</code> — calculations.</li>
              <li><code>:</code> — clipboard history.</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <section id="configuration">
            <span class="section-kicker">User state</span>
            <h2>Configuration</h2>
            <p>Primary settings are persisted in <code>~/.config/raohane/native.json</code>. Custom autostart commands belong in <code>~/.config/raohane/autostart.conf</code>.</p>
            <div class="docs-callout">Prefer changing product settings through Raohane Settings. Direct JSON edits are useful for recovery or development, but malformed values can be normalized during schema upgrades.</div>
          </section>

          <section id="themes">
            <span class="section-kicker">Appearance</span>
            <h2>Themes</h2>
            <p>Raohane ships a shared whole-shell theme system. Bundled palettes include Paper, Sakura, Matcha, Slate, Sand, Sumi and Midnight, alongside the default Raohane direction.</p>
            <div class="code-panel"><pre><code>raohane theme list
raohane theme import FILE
raohane theme export ID FILE
raohane theme remove ID</code></pre></div>
          </section>

          <section id="diagnostics">
            <span class="section-kicker">Recovery</span>
            <h2>Diagnostics</h2>
            <p>Start with the complete doctor report. It checks dependencies, installed runtime integrity, services and shell context.</p>
            <div class="code-panel"><pre><code>raohane doctor all
raohane status
raohane logs</code></pre></div>
            <h3>Inspect startup errors directly</h3>
            <div class="code-panel"><pre><code>raohane stop
raohane run</code></pre></div>
            <p>For performance reports, include the installed version, recent logs, process usage during the issue and the exact interaction that triggered it.</p>
          </section>

          <section id="development">
            <span class="section-kicker">Source</span>
            <h2>Development</h2>
            <p>Product QML lives under <code>modules/raohane/</code>. Static audits validate source/runtime boundaries, but final release validation still requires a real Hyprland + Quickshell session.</p>
            <div class="code-panel"><pre><code>bash scripts/raohane-audit.sh
bash scripts/runtime-payload-audit.sh</code></pre></div>
            <p><a class="button button-ghost" href="https://github.com/killmyselfrin/raohane-dots/tree/main/docs" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open source documentation ↗</a></p>
          </section>
        </article>
      </div>
    </main>
    <SiteFooter />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
